WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.067
Matthew, Chapter Six.

2
00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:08.267
Take heed that ye do not your alms before men, to be seen of them: otherwise ye have no reward of your Father which is in heaven.

3
00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:17.067
Therefore when thou doest thine alms, do not sound a trumpet before thee, as the hypocrites do in the synagogues and in the streets, that they may have glory of men.

4
00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:19.867
Verily I say unto you, They have their reward.

5
00:00:19.867 --> 00:00:32.000
But when thou doest alms, let not thy left hand know what thy right hand doeth: That thine alms may be in secret: and thy Father which seeth in secret himself shall reward thee openly.

6
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:41.200
And when thou prayest, thou shalt not be as the hypocrites are: for they love to pray standing in the synagogues and in the corners of the streets, that they may be seen of men.

7
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.200
Verily I say unto you, They have their reward.

8
00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:56.400
But thou, when thou prayest, enter into thy closet, and when thou hast shut thy door, pray to thy Father which is in secret; and thy Father which seeth in secret shall reward thee openly.

9
00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:04.133
But when ye pray, use not vain repetitions, as the heathen do: for they think that they shall be heard for their much speaking.

10
00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:11.067
Be not ye therefore like unto them: for your Father knoweth what things ye have need of, before ye ask him.

11
00:01:11.067 --> 00:01:17.733
After this manner therefore pray ye: Our Father which art in heaven, Hallowed be thy name.

12
00:01:17.733 --> 00:01:19.200
Thy kingdom come.

13
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:22.000
Thy will be done in earth, as it is in heaven.

14
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.200
Give us this day our daily bread.

15
00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.733
And forgive us our debts, as we forgive our debtors.

16
00:01:27.733 --> 00:01:35.733
And lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from evil: For thine is the kingdom, and the power, and the glory, for ever.

17
00:01:35.733 --> 00:01:36.667
Amen.

18
00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:46.933
For if ye forgive men their trespasses, your heavenly Father will also forgive you: But if ye forgive not men their trespasses, neither will your Father forgive your trespasses.

19
00:01:46.933 --> 00:01:55.467
Moreover when ye fast, be not, as the hypocrites, of a sad countenance: for they disfigure their faces, that they may appear unto men to fast.

20
00:01:55.467 --> 00:01:58.667
Verily I say unto you, They have their reward.

21
00:01:58.667 --> 00:02:11.867
But thou, when thou fastest, anoint thine head, and wash thy face; That thou appear not unto men to fast, but unto thy Father which is in secret: and thy Father, which seeth in secret, shall reward thee openly.

22
00:02:11.867 --> 00:02:28.800
Lay not up for yourselves treasures upon earth, where moth and rust doth corrupt, and where thieves break through and steal: But lay up for yourselves treasures in heaven, where neither moth nor rust doth corrupt, and where thieves do not break through nor steal: For where your treasure is,

23
00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:30.667
there will your heart be also.

24
00:02:30.667 --> 00:02:37.067
The light of the body is the eye: if therefore thine eye be single, thy whole body shall be full of light.

25
00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:41.067
But if thine eye be evil, thy whole body shall be full of darkness.

26
00:02:41.067 --> 00:02:45.600
If therefore the light that is in thee be darkness, how great is that darkness!

27
00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:54.133
No man can serve two masters: for either he will hate the one, and love the other; or else he will hold to the one, and despise the other.

28
00:02:54.133 --> 00:02:56.400
Ye cannot serve God and mammon.

29
00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:05.600
Therefore I say unto you, Take no thought for your life, what ye shall eat, or what ye shall drink; nor yet for your body, what ye shall put on.

30
00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:08.800
Is not the life more than meat, and the body than raiment?

31
00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:17.600
Behold the fowls of the air: for they sow not, neither do they reap, nor gather into barns; yet your heavenly Father feedeth them.

32
00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:19.733
Are ye not much better than they?

33
00:03:19.733 --> 00:03:23.867
Which of you by taking thought can add one cubit unto his stature?

34
00:03:23.867 --> 00:03:26.533
And why take ye thought for raiment?

35
00:03:26.533 --> 00:03:36.933
Consider the lilies of the field, how they grow; they toil not, neither do they spin: And yet I say unto you, That even Solomon in all his glory was not arrayed like one of these.

36
00:03:36.933 --> 00:03:45.333
Wherefore, if God so clothe the grass of the field, which to day is, and to morrow is cast into the oven, shall he not much more clothe you, O ye of little faith?

37
00:03:45.333 --> 00:03:48.267
Therefore take no thought, saying, What shall we eat?

38
00:03:48.267 --> 00:03:49.467
or, What shall we drink?

39
00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:52.133
or, Wherewithal shall we be clothed?

40
00:03:52.133 --> 00:03:58.533
(For after all these things do the Gentiles seek:) for your heavenly Father knoweth that ye have need of all these things.

41
00:03:58.533 --> 00:04:04.933
But seek ye first the kingdom of God, and his righteousness; and all these things shall be added unto you.

42
00:04:04.933 --> 00:04:10.000
Take therefore no thought for the morrow: for the morrow shall take thought for the things of itself.

43
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.800
Sufficient unto the day is the evil thereof.

